A||||10||fierogt88||Searching for a long lost brother...||||5||
Z||000000||fierogt88||02-20-2001||02:48 PM||||Last September my mother passed away, leaving myself and four siblings with almost no other family.  Just prior to her passing she told us that we have an older brother out there somewhere.  He was privately adopted at birth in Wichita Falls, Texas, and he was born on July 8, 1968.  She requested he be named "Ron" after his father, but never knew if this came to be.<P>My siblings and I have begun the search, and since every one here is always so helpful, I thought I would see what you guys would suggest.  All we have is a birthdate, a birthplace and a possible name.  Also both parents were in the Air-Force, and my mother said the father died in a helicoptor crash.  They were stationed at the Air-Force base near Wichita Falls, but I don't recall the name of it.<p>[This message has been edited by fierogt88 (edited 02-20-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||fierojunky||02-20-2001||03:17 PM||||I don't have any info just wanted to wish ya good luck!||||reg||14
Z||000002||hugh||02-21-2001||06:29 AM||||There are surely sites on the internet that do exactly what you want,good luck in your search!||||reg||1
Z||000003||KnightRyder31||02-21-2001||10:44 AM||||Good luck...and sorry to hear about your mother.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierogt88||02-21-2001||11:01 AM||||Is there anyone here from Wichita Falls, Texas?  I would just like some information on what hospitals are there and who to write to and get public records.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Oreif||02-21-2001||11:27 AM||||I don't think birth certificates have adoption information on them but you never know. Sheppard Air Force Base is the one near Wichita Falls, TX. You could try to locate the father by looking for the helicopter crash and seeing who was involved in it. Then once you have the year of the crash and the names you can locate local school records and see who had the same sir name (last name) for the respective age and if the child was removed out of school. If the father died, chances are the mother moved back to her side of the family. The school will have records of where they forwarded the childs school records if they did. The school records will also list the birth date too. Once you have a full name and a location you can look at phone books in the area. Another source is High school reunion sites. If you find the name and location, getting to the H.S. isn't too hard and they can provide reunion lists which have last known address' of the students. It is very time consuming to locate someone but not very difficult. The AFB should be a good place to start. Just call them and let them know exactly what you are looking for and why. Also most cities have their own websites so you should be able to track the schools and public records like birth certificates. Hope this helps or at least gets you started in the right direction.<P>Sorry to hear of your Mother.<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">   <P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Oreif||02-21-2001||11:50 AM||||Found this:<BR>The 3630th Flying Training Wing was activated in 1965, and it assumed the helicopter training program. It began providing undergraduate pilot training in the T-37 and T-38 for the German Air Force in August 1966. Helicopter training was discontinued in 1971 when the U.S. Army assumed responsibility for training Air Force helicopter pilots. <P>So now you have the squadron that did the helicopter training and you know that the crash happened sometime between<BR>July 1968 and 1971. The bad thing is your brother would have been 3 years old or younger so unless they stayed in the area there would not be any school records. You could probably check with the AFB and trace the crash victims to the ones that added a son in 1968 to their dependents records.<P>Just thought of this, the base Hospital may have records of the childs check-ups. So the names can be cross-checked with the crash victims.<P><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 02-21-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierogt88||02-21-2001||04:40 PM||||Thank you.  This should help point me in the right direction.  I'm still looking for someone in Wichita Falls.  I dug up my mothers old address and was hoping someone could verify that it still existed... <P>Does anyone know where I can find contact information for Sheppard Air Force Base?  Also there was a lawyer who handled the "legalities" of the adoption who had his office in Wichita Falls, and did this often for people who were adopting...  Maybe he's still there?<P>Is there any way to get yellow pages on the internet?||||reg||1
Z||000008||JohnnyK||02-21-2001||06:02 PM||||Go to <A HREF="http://www.infospace.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.infospace.com</A>   Should be a good help. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Oreif||02-21-2001||06:24 PM||||Here's the website where you can get information at the AFB. <A HREF="http://www.sheppard.af.mil/locator.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.sheppard.af.mil/locator.htm</A> <BR>Infoseek<BR>or Yahoo have white pages and yellow pages for the U.S.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||02-21-2001||07:19 PM||||Isn't there some site that will give you tons of info on someone if you have their SS#?  Seems like I played around with this once.  It came up with my school records, partial medical history, etc, etc.  I just can't think of the URL.<P>MM||||reg||1
